    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0065" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8890/973¹⁄₆: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-05T10:00:00+04:00">August 5, 1942—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 6—9:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. Please see my next No. 48.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d51-f1"/> … to reciprocating
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">reciprocate?</hi>] numerous recent expressions of
                    good-will towards the United States in connection with the establishment of our
                    Legation here, the Department may wish to recommend that whenever possible a
                    little space on steamers returning to the United States from India be made
                    available for reasonable quantities of Afghan exports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
